<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/14th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">St. George's Night Uprising</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1343">1343</a>–<a href="/years/1345">1345</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as St George's Night Uprising</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">St. George's Night Uprising was a rebellion of the Estonian peasantry in Harju and other districts against their German and Danish lords, begun on the night of 23 April 1343. The rebels killed many Germans and besieged Tallinn but were crushed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a>, after which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> sold its Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonia">Estonia</a> to the Order in 1346.</p></div>
